  "grammar": [
    {
      "title": "Ser for Professions and Identity",
      "content": "Use SER to state your profession or identity.\n\nSoy + profession (NO article):\n- Soy ingeniero. (I'm an engineer.)\n- Soy m\u00e9dico. (I'm a doctor.)\n- Soy profesora. (I'm a teacher.)\n\nNOT 'Soy el ingeniero' \u2014 no article before profession with SER.\n\nExceptions: With adjectives, you use the article:\n- Soy un ingeniero bueno. (I'm a good engineer.)\n- Es una profesora inteligente. (She's an intelligent teacher.)",
      "examples": [
        "Soy abogado. (I'm a lawyer.)\nElla es m\u00e9dica. (She's a doctor.)\nSomos estudiantes. (We're students.)"
      ]
    },
    {
      "title": "Trabajar + en \u2014 To Work At/In/For",
      "content": "TRABAJAR is a regular -AR verb. It uses 'en' to indicate where or for whom you work.\n\nConjugation: yo trabajo, t\u00fa trabajas, \u00e9l trabaja, nosotros trabajamos, vosotros trabaj\u00e1is, ellos trabajan\n\n- Trabajo EN una oficina. (I work IN an office.)\n- Trabajo PARA Google. (I work FOR Google.)\n- Trabajo CON ingenieros. (I work WITH engineers.)\n\nCommon workplace expressions:\n- Estoy trabajando. (I'm working right now.)\n- Voy a trabajar. (I'm going to work.)\n- Tengo trabajo. (I have a job.)\n- No tengo trabajo. (I don't have a job.)",
      "examples": [
        "Trabajo en un hospital. (I work in a hospital.)\nTrabajo para una empresa. (I work for a company.)\nTrabajo con clientes. (I work with clients.)"
      ]
    }
  ],
  "pronunciation": [
    {
      "title": "The Spanish 'R' \u2014 Single vs Double",
      "content": "Spanish has two 'r' sounds that are crucial:\n\nSingle 'r' (tap): Between vowels, quick tap of tongue\n- pero (but) = PEH-roh\n- caro (expensive) = KAH-roh\n- perro (dog) = PEH-rro (WAIT, this is double!)\n\nDouble 'rr' (trill): Rolled, continuous vibration\n- perro (dog) = PEH-rro\n- tierra (land) = TEEH-rrah\n- carretera (highway) = cah-reh-TEH-rah\n\nWord-initial 'r' is always rolled:\n- ropa (clothes) = ROH-pah\n- rojo (red) = ROH-hoh\n- regla (ruler) = REH-glah",
      "examples": [
        "pero (but) = single tap\nperro (dog) = double trill\nropa = rolled at start",
        "trabajar (to work) = trill in middle"
      ]
    }
  ],
  "exercises": [
    {
      "type": "multiple-choice",
      "question": "How do you say 'I'm a doctor' in Spanish?",
      "options": [
        "Soy el doctor",
        "Soy doctor",
        "Estoy doctor",
        "Trabajo doctor"
      ],
      "correct": 1,
      "explanation": "Use SER + profession WITHOUT article: 'Soy doctor'."
    },
    {
      "type": "multiple-choice",
      "question": "What does 'Trabajo en una oficina' mean?",
      "options": [
        "I work in a hospital",
        "I work in an office",
        "I go to an office",
        "I have an office"
      ],
      "correct": 1,
      "explanation": "'Trabajo en una oficina' = I work in an office."
    },
    {
      "type": "fill-in-blank",
      "question": "Complete: 'Soy ___ y trabajo en un banco.' (I'm an engineer and I work at a bank.)",
      "correct": "ingeniero",
      "explanation": "'Ingeniero' = engineer (masculine form)."
    },
    {
      "type": "fill-in-blank",
      "question": "Complete: 'Trabajo ___ una empresa de tecnolog\u00eda.' (I work at a technology company.)",
      "correct": "en",
      "explanation": "'Trabajar en' = to work at/in."
    }
  ]
}
